{"id": "e153", "source": "r1", "locator": "README.md:111", "quote": "- **You have no subagents yet.** Start with one loop. Read `reference_loop/loop.py` and\n  add tools and skills as testing shows you need them.", "why": "subagent 가 아직 없으면 한 loop 로 시작하라는 kit 의 문장"}
{"id": "e154", "source": "w1", "locator": "§How to fold subagents into the main agent loop", "quote": "Many teams already have an orchestrator and a set of specialist agents in production. The following is the single loop design we'd suggest working toward:", "why": "단일 loop 는 이미 multi-agent 가 있는 팀이 향할 목표"}
{"id": "e155", "source": "r1", "locator": "skill/steps/00-audit.md:125", "quote": "- **Worklist**: checkboxes, in this order: merges, then folds, then as-tool changes.", "why": "kit 의 작업 순서: merge, fold, as-tool"}
{"id": "e156", "source": "r1", "locator": "skill/steps/04-as-tool.md:3", "quote": "Use this for a row whose verdict is `as-tool`, and for any subagent that lost its fold\ncomparison.", "why": "fold 비교에서 진 subagent 를 as-tool 로"}
{"id": "e157", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Subagents called as tools", "quote": "This is a good first step, as you don’t need to rewrite the subagents.", "why": "2026-10 글은 as-tool 을 fold 앞의 첫 단계로 둔다"}
{"id": "e158", "source": "w10", "locator": "머리말", "quote": "However, not every complex task requires this approach—a single agent with the right (sometimes dynamic) tools and prompt can often achieve similar results.", "why": "LangChain 문서도 단일 agent 로 충분한 경우가 많다고 먼저 적는다"}
{"id": "e159", "source": "w10", "locator": "§Why multi-agent?", "quote": "Distributed development: Allow different teams to develop and maintain capabilities independently, composing them into a larger system with clear boundaries.", "why": "팀 경계를 multi-agent 의 이유로 드는 업계 문서의 문장"}
{"id": "e160", "source": "w10", "locator": "§Why multi-agent?", "quote": "Multi-agent patterns are particularly valuable when a single agent has too many tools and makes poor decisions about which to use, when tasks require specialized knowledge with extensive context (long prompts and domain-specific tools), or when you need to enforce sequential constraints that unlock capabilities only after certain conditions are met.", "why": "tool 수, 긴 전문 지식을 나누는 이유로 든다"}
{"id": "e161", "source": "w10", "locator": "§Patterns 표", "quote": "Skills | Specialized prompts and knowledge loaded on-demand. A single agent stays in control while loading context from skills as needed.", "why": "LangChain 은 skill 을 multi-agent 패턴의 하나로 이미 싣는다"}
{"id": "e162", "source": "w10", "locator": "§Patterns 표", "quote": "Router | A routing step classifies input and directs it to one or more specialized agents. Results are synthesized into a combined response.", "why": "router 패턴"}
{"id": "e163", "source": "w10", "locator": "§Patterns 표", "quote": "Subagents | A main agent coordinates subagents as tools. All routing passes through the main agent, which decides when and how to invoke each subagent.", "why": "supervisor 를 tool 호출로 하는 subagents 패턴"}
{"id": "e164", "source": "w10", "locator": "§Performance comparison › Multi-domain", "quote": "After loading, every subsequent call processes all 6K tokens of skill documentation. Subagents processes 67% fewer tokens overall due to context isolation. Total: 15K tokens.", "why": "skill 로 한 context 에 싣는 비용을 LangChain 이 숫자로 보인다. 13장 한계"}
{"id": "e165", "source": "w10", "locator": "§Why multi-agent?", "quote": "Context management: Provide specialized knowledge without overwhelming the model’s context window.", "why": "context 관리를 이유로"}
{"id": "e166", "source": "r2", "locator": "README.md:5", "quote": "The supervisor controls all communication flow and task delegation, making decisions about which agent to invoke based on the current context and task requirements.", "why": "LangGraph supervisor 의 정의"}
{"id": "e167", "source": "r2", "locator": "README.md:133", "quote": "You can create multi-level hierarchical systems by creating a supervisor that manages multiple supervisors.", "why": "hierarchical teams"}
{"id": "e168", "source": "r2", "locator": "README.md:3", "quote": "> **Note**: We now recommend using the **supervisor pattern directly via tools** rather than this library for most use cases.", "why": "LangChain 이 supervisor 를 tool 호출로 옮겨 권한다"}
{"id": "e169", "source": "r2", "locator": "README.md:136", "quote": "research_team = create_supervisor(", "why": "팀 단위 supervisor 예"}
{"id": "e170", "source": "w11", "locator": "§Hierarchical Process", "quote": "Emulates a corporate hierarchy, CrewAI allows specifying a custom manager agent or automatically creates one, requiring the specification of a manager language model (manager_llm). This agent oversees task execution, including planning, delegation, and validation.", "why": "CrewAI 의 manager 는 회사 위계를 본뜬다"}
